## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical knowledge of API-layer tenant isolation using common GCP primitives. It tests understanding of JWT validation, IAM Conditions, quotas, logging, and CI validation—all essential skills for building secure multi-tenant SaaS applications.

## Key Concepts
- JWT validation and tenant_id extraction from tokens
- API Gateway configuration with per-tenant quotas and IAM Conditions
- Tenant-specific error handling and observability
- CI gate for synthetic tenants and safe rollback procedures

## Sample Implementation
```javascript
// Verify tenant_id from JWT claims
const verifyTenantAccess = (req, res, next) => {
  const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;
  const token = authHeader?.split(' ')[1];

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    if (!decoded.tenant_id) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Missing tenant_id claim' });
    }
    req.tenant_id = decoded.tenant_id;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
  }
};

// Per-tenant quota check
const checkQuota = async (tenantId) => {
  const limit = await quotaService.getLimit(tenantId);
  const used = await quotaService.getUsage(tenantId);
  if (used >= limit) {
    throw new Error('Quota exceeded');
  }
};

// Tenant-scoped logging
const logWithTenant = (tenantId, action, metadata) => {
  console.log(JSON.stringify({
    tenant_id: tenantId,
    action,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    ...metadata
  }));
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to secure public Cloud Run endpoints for multiple partners using standard GCP controls.

## Key Concepts
- Least-privilege IAM per partner
- IAP for authenticating users to Cloud Run
- Per-partner isolation via separate service accounts or gateway policies
- Credential rotation and auditability
- Synthetic tests to validate misconfig denial

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test: simulate non-permitted access and expect HTTP 403
const token = obtainTokenFor('partnerX');
fetch('https://api.example.run.app/endpoint', { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }})
  .then(response => {
    if (response.status === 403) {
      console.log('✓ Access properly blocked for unauthorized partner');
    } else {
      console.error('✗ Security misconfiguration detected');
    }
  });
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question validates expertise in PKI design, mTLS implementation, and CI/CD containment strategies for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- Private CA hierarchies per tenant for isolation
- mTLS with SPIFFE/SVID for workload identity
- Automated certificate rotation and revocation handling
- CI validation and rollback playbooks
- Observability via Cloud Monitoring, Cloud Logging, and Cloud IDS

## Code Example
```javascript
// CI gate: verify issued certificates include tenantId in SAN
function validateCert(certPem, tenantId) {
  const cert = new X509.Cert(certPem);
  const sans = cert.getSubjectAltName();
  return sans.includes(`tenantId:${tenantId}`);
}

// Validate certificate chain integrity
function validateChain(chainPem) {
  const chain = X509.CertChain.fromPEM(chainPem);
  return chain.verify();
}
```

The code above demonstrates CI-level validation: the first function ensures each certificate contains the tenant identifier in its Subject Alternative Names, enabling tenant-aware access control. The second function verifies the entire certificate chain signature integrity before deployment, preventing compromised or tampered certificates from entering the production mesh.

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in designing tenant-isolated logging architectures—a critical security requirement in multi-tenant SaaS platforms where log exposure can lead to data breaches.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Logging Router with tenant-specific sinks using label-based filtering
- IAM Conditions implementing least-privilege access controls
- Data Loss Prevention API for automatic PII redaction
- CI/CD pipeline integration with synthetic tenant provisioning
- Automated rollback mechanisms for isolation verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// Conceptual tenant sink configuration
const tenantSink = {
  name: `tenant-${tenantId}-sink`,
  filter: `resource.type="cloud_run_revision" AND labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  destination: `bigquery.googleapis.com/projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_logs`
};

// IAM Condition for tenant access
const tenantAccessCondition = {
  title: `Tenant ${tenantId} Log Access`,
  expression: `resource.name.startsWith("projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_")`
};
```
